<onlyinclude>'''Knowledge management''' is the organized practice of creating, locating, sharing, retaining and applying knowledge in an organization or community. It includes people, processes and technology rather than merely storing documents.

== Explanation ==
A team might record how it solved a recurring problem, maintain examples and make experienced people available to answer questions. A useful knowledge-management system keeps the source and scope of advice visible, so others can decide when it applies. Some skills remain difficult to describe in a document.

